From e909b5426261b87623a3972fe5936f8134e85cd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:22:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 206/211] drm/imagination: Add frequency scaling

Scale the core clock and its supply with load the way panfrost does: a
devfreq device driven by the simple_ondemand governor, fed by how long at
least one job has been in flight. Jobs already take a power reference for
exactly that span, so the accounting hangs off that. The device also
registers as a cooling device, so a thermal zone can hold it back.

The firmware keeps its own copy of the core clock for its timers. After
every change write the new rate into the runtime configuration, which it
reads on each boot, and tell a running firmware directly with the clock
speed change command, the same handshake the vendor driver performs.

Everything is keyed off an operating points table in the device tree;
without one nothing changes.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
